{
  "slug": "version-sentinel",
  "name": "Version Sentinel",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Hard-blocks dependency additions, bumps, and downgrades until a fresh, source-cited version check is recorded via WebSearch. Supports npm, pip, Cargo, and NuGet ecosystems. Uses PreToolUse hooks to intercept manifest edits and install commands, blocking them until the developer verifies the latest version upstream.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **1 agent**, **2 commands** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `version-sentinel` (Use when adding, bumping, or changing a dependency in package.json, requirements*.txt, constraints*.txt, pyproject.toml, Cargo.toml, *.csproj, *.fsproj, or *.vbproj)\n- **Agents** (1): `version-reviewer.agent` (Use before tagging a release, merging a release PR, or whenever the user asks to audit dependency freshness)\n- **Commands** (2): `check-versions` (Audit dependencies against upstream registries (npm, pypi, nuget, crates.io)), `vs-record` (Record a fresh version check in the version-sentinel sidecar)\n- **Hooks** (3): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install version-sentinel@claude-community` from `KSEGIT/Version-Sentinel`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 3,
    "command": 2
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
